      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105752,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105753,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PFHTs have a strong predilection for the upper extremities, followed by the lower extremities. Other sites less frequently involved include the trunk&nbsp;/ abdominal wall and the head and neck region {17870015; 2847569; 1723956}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105754,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with PFHT present with a slow-growing tumour or plaque measuring about 25&nbsp;mm (range: 5&ndash;80&nbsp;mm) {10366148; 30145610}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105755,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PFHT shows a wide age range, with a predilection for children and young adults (mean age: ~15&nbsp;years, range: 1&ndash;77&nbsp;years); 50&ndash;70% of cases occur in patients aged &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;years {2847569; 10366148; 17870015}. There is a slight female predominance {2847569; 10366148; 17870015; 30145610}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105756,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105757,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105758,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PFHT is an infiltrative&nbsp;/ poorly defined mass at the dermal&ndash;subcutaneous junction.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105759,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PFHT is localized to the dermal&ndash;subcutaneous junction, with infiltration of subcutaneous adipose tissue and skeletal muscle. The tumour is characterized by a plexiform or multinodular arrangement of nodules of histiocytoid cells with a variable number of admixed multinucleated, osteoclastic-like giant cells, connected by fascicles of spindled fibroblastic/myofibroblastic cells. Other histological changes include chronic inflammation, metaplastic bone, haemorrhage, and haemosiderin deposition. Mild to moderate cytological atypia may be present; marked pleomorphism is rare. The mitotic count is typically low; however, occasional cases contain atypical forms {10366148; 17870015}. Lymphovascular or perineural invasion may rarely be seen {2847569; 10366148; 17870015}. SMA is expressed in the (myo)fibroblastic component.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Those tumours with an overabundance of the (myo)fibroblastic component (e.g. fibroblastic PFHT) may mimic fibromatosis, the recently described plexiform myofibroblastoma {32618598}, plexiform neurofibroma, and fibrous hamartoma of infancy. A prominent fibrohistiocytic pattern may be reminiscent of dermatofibroma, which lacks the plexiform pattern {22420728}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105760,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105761,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105762,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> nodules of histiocytoid cells and often osteoclastic-like giant cells; fascicles of (myo)fibroblastic spindle cells; plexiform architecture.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105763,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105764,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 159,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are associated with a risk of local recurrence (12&ndash;38%), with rare lymph node metastases {2847569; 10366148; 17870015}. Distant metastasis is extremely rare {9130995; 10366148}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T12:28:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]